WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.488
Step three plans, as a dry run.

2
00:00:02.488 --> 00:00:06.259
You give it the cloud, the
fixture estate, the desired state,

3
00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:09.952
the principal I D of the identity
that would run the apply,

4
00:00:09.952 --> 00:00:14.274
so it can flag that identity's own
roles, an output folder and a run I D.

5
00:00:14.274 --> 00:00:18.384
It reads nine assignment schedules
and two eligibility schedules,

6
00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.512
and twelve policies at four scopes.

7
00:00:20.512 --> 00:00:25.009
The plan: eleven policy updates,
five eligible assignments to add,

8
00:00:25.009 --> 00:00:27.924
and three standing assignments to remove.

9
00:00:27.924 --> 00:00:30.287
Nineteen requests, in that order.

10
00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:34.850
The findings: seven, with two
warnings and one information item.

11
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.468
It's a dry run, so the
nineteen requests are

12
00:00:37.468 --> 00:00:40.087
written to the plan
file, and none are sent.

13
00:00:40.087 --> 00:00:42.840
Review the diff, then
run again with Apply.
